  "21": {
   "index": 21,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "The results were 59.5% desired “occasional boxed text,” 34.4% “lots of boxed text,” and only 6% of respondents did not want any boxed text.",
   "note": "All three figures and the phrase 'occasional boxed text' verbatim. Attribution confirmed: 'A Twitter poll by D&D's current lead rules designer Jeremy Crawford saw 2,248 replies to the question “How much boxed text (aka read-aloud text) do you like in an adventure you run?”' (endnote 38 cites @JeremyECrawford, 17 Nov 2016). The claim's 'about 6%' matches 'only 6%'.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-chunk-01.json"
  },
  "22": {
   "index": 22,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "read aloud text that the DM is instructed to read to the players. Often these passages describe the location, but sometimes they are also used to describe the action of NPCs",
