  "66": {
   "index": 66,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "In 4E, we used \"save\" as a synonym for \"successful saving throw.\" We have abandoned that practice.",
   "note": "Quote 'We have abandoned that practice' appears verbatim TWICE on p.6, once in each named place. Minor precision point, not an unsupported limb: the guide attributes the 'result' usage to '3E and 4E', not 4E alone — 'In 3E and 4E, the word \"result\" was sometimes used as a synonym for \"the number rolled on a die.\"' The 'save' usage is attributed to 4E alone, as claimed.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i64-78.json"
  },
  "67": {
   "index": 67,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "Avoid referring to points of damage. ... And \"magic item\" and its variants should never be \"magical item.\"",
   "note": "All three limbs verbatim. p.6 'Points of Damage': 'write, \"The spell deals 10 fire damage,\" not \"The spell deals 10 points of fire damage.\"'; p.7 'Hit Point Maximum': 'When you write about a creature's hit point maximum, avoid \"maximum hit points.\"'; p.6 '\"Magic\" vs. \"Magical\"': '\"magic item\" and its variants should never be \"magical item.\"' Page citation pp.6-7 is correct.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i64-78.json"
  },
  "68": {
