   "note": "Claim carries no quote field, and its parenthetical inverts the guide's word order (guide: 'the wall of fire spell produces a wall of fire'; claim: 'the spell wall of fire produces a wall of fire') — hence SUBSTANCE, not VERBATIM. Every listed term is on p.5 'Formatting Game Terms': Terms to Capitalize lists Ability scores, Armor Class, Artifacts, Class features, Difficulty Class, Dungeon Master, Feats, Languages, Planes of existence, Skills, 'Traits in races and monsters'; Terms to Italicize lists Artifacts, Magic items, Spells; and 'The italicized terms are treated as titles, even when they don't use title capitalization.'",
