   "index": 69,
   "verdict": "PARTIAL",
   "trueWording": "this subhead should be followed by terminal punctuation, not a colon",
   "note": "Quote verbatim on p.2. Limbs: 'The lowest level of our heading hierarchy is the inline subhead. It functions as our heading 4.'; the correct example is verbatim 'Keen Senses. You have proficiency in the Perception skill.' (with the colon version shown as incorrect); and 'Don't confuse an inline subhead with the bolded title of a stat block entry or other data field.' One nuance on the bold-italics limb: it is the guide's fallback instruction, not unconditional — 'If you don't have access to the style, set the subhead in bold italics to distinguish it from text that is simply bold.'",
   "unsupportedLimb": "bold italics is the guide's conditional fallback ('If you don't have access to the style, set the subhead in bold italics'), not the unconditional rule the claim states",
