   "note": "Quote verbatim on p.7, section 'Avoid \"Week\" and \"Month\"'. Limbs: 'A week is ten days long in the Forgotten Realms, for instance, and is called a tenday.'; 'don't express durations or other lengths of time in weeks or months when you're writing rules'; 'The length of the year varies as well, but you may use years for durations and the like.' One nuance: the guide's stated reason is broader than the claim's — 'The lengths of weeks and months vary in different D&D worlds', with the Realms tenday given as an instance.",
