  "74": {
   "index": 74,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "We write \"fifth edition,\" for instance, not \"5th Edition.\"",
   "note": "Claim carries no quote field, but all three of its inline quoted strings are verbatim on pp.1-2: 'In a departure from previous usage, we spell out and lowercase references to editions of the roleplaying game. We write \"fifth edition,\" for instance, not \"5th Edition.\" We prefer to use an edition designation as a modifier of another term—\"the fifth edition Dungeon Master's Guide,\" for example.' The 'switches' limb is machine-confirmed by diff: v1.04a contains '5th Edition' and not 'fifth edition' (its edition list reads '1st Edition ... 5th Edition'); v1.08a's list reads 'first edition ... fifth edition'.",
