   "verdict": "PARTIAL",
   "trueWording": "Avoid gender-specific suffixes whenever possible.",
   "note": "Quote verbatim on p.3. Limbs verbatim: 'we write \"priest\" or \"actor\" whether the person is male or female'; 'use \"god\" whether the deity is male or female. Again, in-world uses of \"goddess\" are fine.' The '-ess only in in-world titles' limb is very slightly compressed — the guide's condition is 'only if it's part of a person's title or an in-world organizations' titles', i.e. a person's title as well as an organization's. Section is new in v1.08a: 'gender-specific suffixes' is absent from v1.04a.",
   "unsupportedLimb": "the '-ess only in in-world titles' condition is compressed: the guide's condition is 'only if it's part of a person's title or an in-world organizations' titles'",
