  "77": {
   "index": 77,
   "verdict": "PARTIAL",
   "trueWording": "WotC doesn't bother to make sure their hardcovers follow the guidelines",
   "note": "Raw thread HTML fetched (200, 167KB). Post #8 by pukunui, timestamped 2018-11-27 in the page's own <time datetime> attributes (thread opened 2018-11-25), reads: 'There's some great stuff in the FR style guide. It's a real shame WotC doesn't bother to make sure their hardcovers follow the guidelines (e.g. The style guide says \"week\" is banned and one should use \"tenday\" instead, but \"week\" shows up in FR products all the time!)'. Poster, ban, tenday and hardcover-violation limbs all present verbatim; the claim's closing gloss 'house style is aspirational, not uniformly applied' is the compiler's paraphrase of that sentence rather than the poster's wording, hence SUBSTANCE. Note the poster attributes the rule to the FR style guide specifically.",
