  "82": {
   "index": 82,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "Your Speed is 0 and can't increase",
   "note": "Raw page read via curl. Quote verbatim: 'Any condition that had \"can't move\", was changed to \"Your Speed is 0 and can't increase.\"' Standardization further supported by 'can't speak' being consolidated into Incapacitated. INFLUENCE and STUDY each flagged '(This is a new action.)'; UTILIZE 'is a renaming of the old \"Use an Object\" action'; 'D20 TEST: This is a simple new definition that they have added.' Capitalization of the action names is shown by the page's own usage (e.g. 'now called D20 Tests', 'Heavily Obscured', 'Hide check') and its all-caps headings rather than asserted outright.",
