   "note": "Raw page read via curl. Both quotes verbatim: 'Crawford states that the new Player's Handbook will start by \"teaching you how to play\" DnD' and 'The current Player's Handbook jumps right into character creation'. How to Play chapter named ('The art in the How to Play chapter'). Two-column annotation verbatim: 'Text examples use a two-column format, with the left of the page used for a dialogue between players during a game, and rules commentary boxes on the right explaining what rules are in play in the example.' Attribution nuance: 'jumps right into character creation' is the Wargamer writer's own sentence, not a Crawford quote - do not cite it as his words.",
