   "trueWording": "trying to recapture the campaign instead of the scenario",
   "note": "Raw page fetched (HTTP 200). 'Ptolus: Running the Campaign - From Table to Page', January 5th, 2018, The Alexandrian. Quote verbatim; it is introduced as what you must be wary of when going table-to-page, i.e. adapting his own home campaign (The Complex of Zombies) into a publishable scenario, and the following paragraphs give the falls-in-love-with-an-NPC example. Warning limb supported.",
