   "note": "Raw page fetched (HTTP 200). Quote verbatim in the final substantive paragraph of the Peterson excerpt; the same sentence ties Keep on the Borderlands (B2), shipped with the Moldvay Basic Set, to the height of the D&D boom in 1981. Page is introduced as a never-before-seen piece cut from Peterson's Game Wizards, so the attribution to Peterson holds.",
