   "trueWording": "“this town hates this town over here”",
   "note": "Raw page fetched (HTTP 200). Quote verbatim, spoken by Zeb Cook in the exchange on conflict, about the worst worldbuilding books being 'literally just lists of places and people'. The claim's 'never saying' renders the page's 'They don't spend any time saying', and 'the town next to it' renders 'this town over here'.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i796-842.json"
  },
  "833": {
   "index": 833,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "“You are not creating a world for yourself”",
   "note": "Raw page fetched (HTTP 200). Quote verbatim, Cook speaking, prefaced by 'if I'm doing something for publication', which supports the claim's 'published'; the next sentence supplies the 'for other players to take and use' limb. The citation's page field says 'exchange on choosing a theme'; the actual context is the exchange on deciding what to work on and for whom.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i796-842.json"
  },
  "834": {
   "index": 834,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "“needs to be super clear what kind of adventures take place”",
   "note": "Raw page fetched (HTTP 200). Quote verbatim, twice (body and pull-quote), spoken by Richard Green. The claim's 'at once' renders the page's condition 'when you pick up a new game or a new setting book'; the sentence continues with what the characters are going to get up to.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i796-842.json"
  },
