   "trueWording": "",
   "note": "S-BOUND: the feature already has three or more verified independent sources; not verified this round",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-triage-r10.json"
  },
  "1113": {
   "index": 1113,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "Absolutist statements are, instead, editorial nightmares.",
   "note": "Live chrisssims.wordpress.com fetched 200 (raw HTML). Closing sentence of a paragraph under 'Superlatives or Absolutisms'; the same paragraph supplies the causal limb, saying that in a shared universe of fiction or game design an absolute statement paints further creation into a corner.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i1056-1130.json"
  },
  "1114": {
   "index": 1114,
   "verdict": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM",
   "trueWording": "I call this problem the “flat-culture issue.”",
   "note": "Same raw page. Under the 'Generalizations' heading; the preceding clause names the problem as homogeny among imaginary people, and the next sentences credit Eberron's sophisticated takes but say it fails to escape the flat-culture issue with much of its reimagining. Every limb supported.",
   "fromFile": "verdicts-dnd-i1056-1130.json"
  },
